## On every pull request

| Workflow | What it does |
|---|---|
| `ci.yml` (Server Tests) | Runs `compileall` and a merge-conflict-marker scan. `.github/helper/install.sh` builds a frappe-bench with frappe and erpnext on the **same branch name as the PR base**, plus `payments`, and installs `healthcare` on `test_site` (MariaDB 11.8). Then `bench run-parallel-tests --app healthcare`. Skipped when a PR changes only `css/js/md/html/csv`. Ignores `version-*-beta` branches. 30-minute timeout. |
| `linters.yml` / `linters.v2.yml` | `pre-commit` (ruff, ruff-format, prettier, eslint, pip-audit, detect-secrets, file checks) plus **semgrep** with frappe/semgrep-rules and `r/python.lang.correctness`. v2 also runs on push. |
| `semantic-commits.yml` | commitlint over every commit in the PR. |
| `docs_checker.yml` | `feat` PRs need a wiki docs link (or `no-docs`). |
| `labeller.yml` | Auto-labels PRs. |
| `codeql.yml` | CodeQL for python and javascript on develop pushes and PRs, plus a weekly run. |

Nightly at 00:00 UTC, `ci.yml` also runs with coverage and uploads it to **Codecov** (patch target 85%, project threshold 0.5%).

## Merge

Mergify merges after at least 1 approval and green CI. The `squash` label switches to squash merge, and `dont-merge` blocks merging. Backport labels open backport PRs automatically.

## Release

1. **Weekly, Tuesday 09:30 UTC**, `initiate_release.yml` opens `chore: release v1x` PRs from `version-1x-hotfix` into `version-1x` for 14, 15, and 16.
2. A push to `version-14/15/16` triggers `on_release.yml`, which runs **semantic-release** (`.releaserc`, angular preset; breaking changes do not trigger a major bump). It bumps the version in `healthcare/__init__.py`, commits `chore(release): Bumped to Version x.y.z`, and creates a GitHub release.
3. `release_notes.yml` regenerates the notes and strips `chore`/`ci`/`test`/`docs`/`style` entries.
4. **Weekly, Sunday 09:30 UTC**, `generate-pot-file.yml` regenerates the translation template on `develop`. Crowdin opens `fix: sync translations from crowdin` PRs.

There is no deploy step in the repo. Sites deploy by `bench get-app` / `bench update` (or Frappe Cloud). Several workflows still hard-code `earthians/biograph` and its secrets, so release automation may not run in this fork.
